{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-14T08:15:28.645Z","data":{"text":"Done. Here's a summary of the work.\n\n## What I did\n\nCreated `packages/ui/src/change/page-model.ts`, the pure change-page model required by web-inspection \"Change page model\":\n\n- **`changePage(change)`** → `{ state, label, summary, main, second }`. `state` is `rejected` for a rejected location, else `unknown` with no `nextStep`, else `revised` when a `dead` next step meets a `ready` `autoSteer`, else `nextStep.state`. Every row of the requirement's table is implemented, with the `task`/`tasks` noun rule.\n- **`progressLine(change)`** → the first running task's `Task <n> of <m> running · <elapsed>`, where elapsed is `<s>s`, `<m> min` from 60s, or `unavailable`; otherwise `<k> of <m> tasks done`.\n- **`haltFacts(change)`** → the first dead/regressed task's heading, reason (or `unavailable`), and `Touched:` paths; otherwise `The change stopped` plus `nextStep.detail`.\n- **`landLine(land)`** → halt, then sync stop, then the first failed gate (`Task <n>`/`Verify`/`Check`/`Validator`), then `No gates recorded`, then `All <g> gate(s) passed`.\n- **`landedLine(change)`** → `<n> tasks, <f> first try`.\n\nThe module imports only `LandView` and `WebChange` types from `../contracts.js`, with no I/O, clock or React, and each exported function carries its `@scenario web-inspection: …` line plus `@adr 013`.\n\nCreated `tests/ui-page-model.test.tsx` with one plain `node:test` block per table row/case of \"Page per state\", \"Progress line\", \"Halt facts\", \"Land line\" and \"Landed line\", taking every expected value from the scenario tables and THENs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Task verify: `tests/ui-page-model.test.tsx` — 24 tests, 0 failures.\n- Proposal verify: `pnpm verify` — typechecks, build, all tests and lint pass.\n- `tests/ui-change.test.tsx`'s source scan accepts the new 215-line file.\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/192-change-page-phone/.run/results/2.md`. No files outside scope were changed and no git commands were run.\n\nTouched: `packages/ui/src/change/page-model.ts`, `tests/ui-page-model.test.tsx`"}}
